AnimeRift manual dependency catalog

This project purposely avoids unnecessary external libraries. The code uses Android framework APIs and AndroidX AppCompat support where required.

1) AndroidX AppCompat (required)
- Library name: androidx.appcompat:appcompat
- Purpose: Required for AppCompatActivity and compatible Android UI behavior.
- Recommended version: 1.7.0
- Official download page: https://developer.android.com/jetpack/androidx/releases/appcompat
- Direct AAR: https://dl.google.com/android/maven2/androidx/appcompat/appcompat/1.7.0/appcompat-1.7.0.aar
- Transitive dependencies: annotation, core, fragment, activity, appcompat-resources, drawables, arch-core, lifecycle, collection, customview, drawerlayout, savedstate, viewpager2, etc.
- Minimum Android: API 23+ recommended
- Java and Android 11: Yes
- 32-bit ARM support: Yes, when the AAR is packaged in an APK targeting armeabi-v7a
- AndroidX / SDK: Yes
- Manual installation: Download the AAR, add it to the Android project libraries/classpath, and ensure the project references AndroidX.
- Required or optional: Required for the current code path.

2) AndroidX Core (required transitively)
- Library name: androidx.core:core
- Purpose: Runtime and utility support used by AndroidX components.
- Recommended version: 1.13.1 or newer compatible with the project
- Official download page: https://developer.android.com/jetpack/androidx/releases/core
- Direct AAR: https://dl.google.com/android/maven2/androidx/core/core/1.13.1/core-1.13.1.aar
- Transitive dependencies: annotations, collection, lifecycle-runtime, etc.
- Minimum Android: API 23+
- Java and Android 11: Yes
- 32-bit ARM support: Yes
- AndroidX / SDK: Yes
- Manual installation: Install as part of the AndroidX dependency set.
- Required or optional: Required transitively.

3) Optional advanced player library
- Library name: com.google.android.exoplayer:exoplayer
- Purpose: Advanced media playback when native VideoView is insufficient for a specific format.
- Recommended version: 2.19.1
- Official download page: https://github.com/google/ExoPlayer/releases
- Direct AAR: https://repo1.maven.org/maven2/com/google/android/exoplayer/exoplayer/2.19.1/exoplayer-2.19.1.aar
- Transitive dependencies: exoplayer-core, exoplayer-dash, exoplayer-hls, exoplayer-smoothstreaming, exoplayer-ui, etc. depending on configuration.
- Minimum Android: API 23+ with AndroidX support
- Java and Android 11: Yes
- 32-bit ARM support: Yes, when built for the target architecture
- AndroidX / SDK: Yes
- Manual installation: Only add after confirming the stream format and legal access rights.
- Required or optional: Optional, not required for the current working version.

4) Optional network client
- Library name: com.squareup.okhttp3:okhttp
- Purpose: Remote source validation or HTTP requests in a future source-provider layer.
- Recommended version: 4.12.0
- Official download page: https://square.github.io/okhttp/
- Direct JAR: https://repo1.maven.org/maven2/com/squareup/okhttp3/okhttp/4.12.0/okhttp-4.12.0.jar
- Transitive dependencies: okio and Kotlin stdlib metadata depending on packaging; review carefully before integrating
- Minimum Android: API 23+
- Java and Android 11: Yes, but better reviewed for Java-native use and Android compatibility
- 32-bit ARM support: Yes, if packaged correctly
- AndroidX / SDK: No additional SDK requirement beyond Android platform tools
- Manual installation: Download the JAR and add to the project manually.
- Required or optional: Optional, not used by the current source.

5) Optional metadata parser
- Library name: com.google.code.gson:gson
- Purpose: JSON parsing for future authorized anime metadata APIs.
- Recommended version: 2.11.0
- Official download page: https://github.com/google/gson/releases
- Direct JAR: https://repo1.maven.org/maven2/com/google/code/gson/gson/2.11.0/gson-2.11.0.jar
- Transitive dependencies: None beyond the JAR itself
- Minimum Android: API 23+
- Java and Android 11: Yes
- 32-bit ARM support: Yes
- AndroidX / SDK: No
- Manual installation: Add the JAR to the project library classpath manually.
- Required or optional: Optional, not used by the current source.

Important notes
- The current code intentionally uses the Android framework first and avoids advanced dependencies unless absolutely necessary.
- No library is auto-configured by this repository.
- Any future library must be manually added and documented in this file before being used in production.
- DRM-protected, paid, or unauthorized media content must never be downloaded or played without proper authorization.
